  "Specification": "This module defines an abstract syntax tree encoded as TLA+ data for a uniprocess PlusCal-style algorithm named Euclid. The AST describes declarations for initial values u_ini and v_ini chosen from 1..MaxNum, variables u and v initialized from them, and a loop that repeatedly updates the variables using a conditional swap and subtraction pattern, followed by an assertion that v equals GCD(u_ini, v_ini). The file does not define an executable transition-system specification, temporal behavior, or fault model; instead it represents program structure as records, tuples, strings, and sequences inside TLA+ values.",
